Overview
This simulator provides a comprehensive platform for:
•	Multi-Satellite Constellation Management: Configure and manage up to 20 satellites in various orbital configurations
•	Realistic Fault Injection: Simulate hardware failures including encoder drift, mechanical friction, power limitations, and battery degradation
•	Advanced Visualization: Generate Unity-compatible binary files for 3D visualization in Vizard
•	Data Analysis: Comprehensive plotting and telemetry logging for performance evaluation
•	Mission Planning: Test fault tolerance and recovery strategies for satellite constellations

Key Features
🌍 Constellation Management
•	Support for multiple orbital configurations (LEO, MEO, GEO)
•	Quick-setup presets for common constellation patterns
•	Individual satellite parameter customization
•	Real-time orbital propagation using Basilisk dynamics

🔧 Fault Simulation
•	Friction Fault: Simulates bearing degradation and mechanical wear
•	Power Limit Fault: Models power system constraints and failures
•	Encoder Fault: Introduces measurement errors in reaction wheel feedback
•	Battery Fault: Simulates battery degradation and increased power consumption

📊 Analysis Tools
•	Real-time plotting of spacecraft dynamics
•	Attitude error analysis
•	Reaction wheel performance monitoring
•	Power consumption tracking
•	Inter-satellite distance calculations

🎮 Visualization
•	Vizard-compatible binary file generation
•	Configurable camera views for each satellite
•	Ground target tracking visualization
•	Orbit trajectory display

System Requirements
Prerequisites
•	Python: 3.7 or higher
•	Basilisk: Latest version properly installed
•	Operating System: Windows 10/11, macOS, or Linux
•	RAM: Minimum 8GB (16GB recommended for large constellations)
•	Storage: At least 2GB free space for simulation outputs

System Requirements
Prerequisites
