Python Dependencies
numpy>=1.19.0
matplotlib>=3.3.0
tkinter (usually included with Python)
Pillow>=8.0.0

Installation
1.	Clone the Repository
git clone <https://github.com/CompProjectA/satelliteConstellation-basilisk.git>
cd satelliteConstellation-basilisk/ProjectWork/BskSim

2.	Verify Basilisk Installation
python -c "from Basilisk import __path__; print('Basilisk found at:', __path__[0])"

3.	Install Additional Dependencies
pip install numpy matplotlib Pillow

4.	Test Installation
cd core
python run_fault_simulator.py

Directory Structure
BskSim/
├── BSK_masters.py              # Master simulation orchestrator
├── README.md                   # This documentation file
│
├── core/                       # Core simulation modules
│   ├── __pycache__/           # Python bytecode cache
│   ├── gui_tab/               # GUI tab implementations
│   │   ├── __init__.py        # Package initialization
│   │   ├── base_tab.py        # Base class for GUI tabs
│   │   ├── constellation_tab.py # Satellite constellation management
│   │   ├── fault_tab.py       # Fault configuration interface
│   │   ├── output_tab.py      # Output settings and logging
│   │   ├── results_tab.py     # Results viewing and analysis
│   │   ├── target_tab.py      # Ground target management
│   │   └── visualization_tab.py # 3D visualization settings
│   │
│   ├── fault_loader.py        # Dynamic fault module loader
│   ├── plots.py              # Centralized plotting engine
│   ├── run_fault_simulator.py # Application entry point
│   ├── rw_fault_help.py      # Help documentation system
│   ├── spacecraft_simulation.py # Core simulation engine
│   ├── spacecraft_simulator_gui.py # Main GUI application
│   ├── style.py              # GUI theme and styling
│   └── swinburne.png         # University logo
│
├── faults/                    # Fault implementation modules
│   ├── __pycache__/          # Python bytecode cache
│   ├── battery_fault.py      # Battery degradation simulation
│   ├── encoder_fault.py      # Encoder error simulation
│   ├── friction_fault.py     # Mechanical friction simulation
│   ├── powerlimit_fault.py   # Power constraint simulation
│   └── rw_fault.py          # Legacy compatibility layer
│
├── logs/                      # Simulation output logs
│   └── sim_results_*/        # Timestamped result directories
│
├── models/                    # Basilisk model configurations
│   ├── __pycache__/          # Python bytecode cache
│   ├── BSK_Dynamics.py       # Spacecraft dynamics models
│   ├── BSK_FormationDynamics.py # Formation flying dynamics
│   ├── BSK_FormationFsw.py   # Formation control algorithms
│   └── BSK_Fsw.py           # Spacecraft control software
│
├── plots/                     # Generated visualization plots
│   └── *.png                 # Timestamped plot images
│
├── plotting/                  # Plotting utility modules
│   ├── __pycache__/          # Python bytecode cache
│   └── BSK_Plotting.py       # Basilisk plotting utilities
│
├── scenarios/                 # Pre-configured scenarios
│   └── (scenario files)      # Example mission scenarios
│
└── Vizfile/                  # Vizard visualization data
    └── _VizFiles/            # Binary visualization files
        └── *_UnityViz.bin    # Vizard-compatible binaries


Quick Start Guide
Launch the Simulator
cd core
python run_fault_simulator.py


Basic Workflow
1.	Configure Constellation: Use the "4-Sat Default" button for a quick start
2.	Add a Fault: Enable friction fault on Satellite1 at 30 minutes
3.	Assign Targets: Click "Auto-Assign All Targets"
4.	Run Simulation: Click the green "Run Simulation" button
5.	View Results: Check the Results tab for generated plots

GUI User Guide
🛰️ Constellation Tab
Manage your satellite constellation with these features:
•	Quick Setup Buttons: Pre-configured constellation patterns 
o	4-Sat Default: 4 satellites at 600km altitude
o	6-Sat MEO: 6 satellites at 1200km altitude
o	2-Sat High: 2 satellites at 2000km altitude
•	Orbit Management: Create custom orbits with specific parameters
•	Satellite List: View and edit individual satellite properties
•	Orbital Parameters: Adjust semi-major axis, eccentricity, inclination, etc.

🔧 Fault Configuration Tab
Configure reaction wheel faults:
•	Fault Type Selection: Choose from friction, power limit, encoder, or battery faults
•	Target Selection: Specify which satellite and reaction wheel
•	Timing Control: Set when the fault occurs during simulation
•	Magnitude Setting: Control fault severity
•	Periodic Faults: Enable recurring fault patterns

🎯 Targets Tab
Manage ground observation targets:
•	Target List: Add/remove observation locations
•	Geographic Coordinates: Set latitude/longitude for each target
•	Priority Assignment: Rank targets by importance (1-5)
•	Satellite Assignment: Link targets to specific satellites
•	Coverage Analysis: Check target visibility from assigned satellites

🎥 Visualization Tab
Configure 3D visualization settings:
•	Camera Configuration: Set camera position and field of view
•	View Presets: Quick camera positions (Earth View, Target View, etc.)
•	Orbit Display: Control orbit line visibility and styling
•	Satellite Display: Adjust spacecraft size and labeling
•	Color Schemes: Choose visualization color themes

📊 Output Settings Tab
Control simulation parameters and outputs:
•	Simulation Duration: Set total runtime (10-90 minutes)
•	Output Options: Enable/disable plots and binary files
•	Directory Configuration: Set output paths for logs and plots
•	Real-time Logging: Monitor simulation progress
•	Binary Filename: Name your Vizard visualization file

📈 Results Tab
Analyze simulation outputs:
•	Plot Browser: Navigate generated visualizations
•	Interactive Viewing: Zoom, pan, and export plots
•	Plot Categories: 
o	Constellation orbit visualizations
o	Inter-satellite distances
o	Fault impact analysis
o	Reaction wheel performance
o	Power consumption tracking

Simulation Workflow
1. Pre-Simulation Setup
Configure Constellation → Define Orbits → Add Satellites
                      ↓
               Set Fault Parameters
                      ↓
              Assign Ground Targets
                      ↓
           Configure Visualization Settings

2. Simulation Execution

Initialize Dynamics → Inject Faults → Propagate Orbits
                   ↓
            Record Telemetry
                   ↓
         Generate Visualization Data

3. Post-Simulation Analysis

Generate Plots → Export Data → Create Vizard Binary
             ↓
      Analyze Fault Impact
             ↓
    Review Performance Metrics


Fault Types
Friction Fault
•	Physical Model: Increases Coulomb friction coefficient
•	Effect: Reduced reaction wheel efficiency, increased power consumption
•	Parameters: 
o	Magnitude: Additional friction torque (N⋅m)
o	Typical values: 0.0001 - 0.001 N⋅m

Power Limit Fault
•	Physical Model: Constrains maximum motor torque
•	Effect: Reduced control authority, slower maneuvers
•	Parameters: 
o	Magnitude: Maximum power limit (W)
o	Typical values: 0.1 - 5.0 W

Encoder Fault
•	Physical Model: Introduces measurement noise/bias
•	Effect: Control oscillations, pointing errors
•	Parameters: 
o	Magnitude: Error percentage (%)
o	Typical values: 5 - 50%

Battery Fault
•	Physical Model: Increases power consumption rate
•	Effect: Reduced mission duration, potential safe mode
•	Parameters: 
o	Magnitude: Additional power drain (W)
o	Typical values: 10 - 100 W

Output Files
Log Files
Location: logs/sim_results_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS/
•	simulation_summary.txt: Configuration and results overview
•	telemetry_*.csv: Time-series spacecraft data
•	fault_log.txt: Fault injection timeline

Plot Files
Location: plots/
•	*_ConstellationAnalysis.png: Orbital configuration
•	*_FaultAnalysis.png: Fault impact visualization
•	*_InterSatelliteDistances.png: Formation geometry
•	*_PowerAnalysis.png: Power system performance

Vizard Files
Location: Vizfile/_VizFiles/
•	*_UnityViz.bin: 3D visualization binary
•	Compatible with Basilisk Vizard application


Troubleshooting – Common Issues and Solutions

GUI does not launch
➤ Verify tkinter installation: python -m tkinter

Basilisk import error
➤ Check PYTHONPATH includes Basilisk directory

Visualization not working
➤ Ensure Vizard is installed and binary path is correct

Memory error with large constellations
➤ Reduce simulation duration or number of satellites

Plots not generating
➤ Check matplotlib backend: use 'Agg' for headless systems

Fault not appearing
➤ Verify fault time is within simulation duration


Technical Architecture
Core Components
1.	Simulation Engine (spacecraft_simulation.py) 
o	Integrates Basilisk dynamics
o	Manages time propagation
o	Handles fault injection events
2.	GUI Framework (spacecraft_simulator_gui.py) 
o	Tkinter-based interface
o	Model-View pattern
o	Event-driven architecture
3.	Fault System (fault_loader.py) 
o	Dynamic module loading
o	Plugin architecture for new fault types
o	Real-time fault injection
4.	Visualization Pipeline 
o	Matplotlib for 2D plots
o	Vizard binary generation for 3D
o	Real-time data streaming capability


Data Flow
User Input → GUI → Configuration → Simulation Engine
                                        ↓
                              Basilisk Dynamics
                                        ↓
                              Fault Injection
                                        ↓
Results ← Plotting Engine ← Data Recording


